[38;2;124;124;124m**Theorem**: If ZFC + I_n is consistent for n ∈ {0, 1, 2}, then ZFC + I_n + GCH [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis consistent. In particular, ZFC + I_n + CH is consistent.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Proof**: We show that GCH can be forced while preserving each I_n axiom. Since[0m[38;2;124;124;124mGCH implies CH, this also gives consistency with CH.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**General strategy**: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Start with a model V ⊨ ZFC + I_n.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. Force GCH using a two-step approach:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   a. Force GCH below the critical point of the embedding (a small forcing that [0m[38;2;124;124;124mdoesn't affect the embedding).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   b. Force GCH at and above the critical point using a reverse Easton iteration[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthat lifts the embedding.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. Show that the embedding lifts through the forcing, preserving I_n.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Case I_2** (j: V → M, crit(j) = κ, λ = sup_n j^n(κ), M^λ ⊆ M):[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mStep 1: Force GCH below κ. Let P₀ be the canonical GCH forcing below κ (a set [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mforcing of size < κ). Since j is the identity on V_κ, j(P₀) = P₀, and the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124membedding lifts trivially through P₀. Let V₁ = V[G₀] where G₀ is P₀-generic. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThen V₁ ⊨ I_2 with the lifted embedding j: V₁ → M₁ (where M₁ = M[G₀]).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mStep 2: Force GCH at and above κ. Define the reverse Easton iteration P₁ in V₁: [0m[38;2;124;124;124mat each regular cardinal α ≥ κ, force with the canonical GCH forcing at α [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(collapsing 2^α to α^+ if needed, or adding subsets if needed). The iteration [0m
[38;2;124;124;124muses Easton support.[0m

