[38;2;124;124;124mforcing of size at most ℵ₁ (either adding ℵ₁ Cohen reals or collapsing 2^{ℵ₀} to[0m[38;2;124;124;124mℵ₁). Since ℵ₁ < κ, this forcing lies entirely below the critical point, where j [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis the identity. The embedding is therefore unaffected, and I_n is preserved. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mHence ZFC + I_n + CH is consistent (relative to ZFC + I_n).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Main argument: GCH is consistent with I_0, I_1, I_2.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe use a two-stage forcing:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- **Stage 1.** Force GCH below the critical point κ of the embedding. This is a [0m[38;2;124;124;124mset forcing of size < κ. Since j is the identity on V_κ, the forcing is fixed by[0m[38;2;124;124;124mj, and the embedding lifts trivially.[0m

