[38;2;124;124;124mHere's my final proof:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m---[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Theorem.** For each n ∈ {0, 1, 2}, if ZFC + I_n is consistent, then ZFC + I_n [0m[38;2;124;124;124m+ GCH is consistent. In particular, ZFC + I_n + CH is consistent.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Proof.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe show that GCH can be forced over any model of I_n while preserving the large [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcardinal embedding. Since GCH implies CH, consistency with GCH entails [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconsistency with CH.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Definitions.** Recall the rank-into-rank axioms:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- I_2: There exists an elementary embedding j: V → M with crit(j) = κ, λ = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msup_{n<ω} jⁿ(κ), and M^λ ⊆ M.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- I_1: There exists a nontrivial elementary embedding j: V_{λ+1} → V_{λ+1}.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- I_0: There exists a nontrivial elementary embedding j: L(V_{λ+1}) → L(V_{λ+1})[0m[38;2;124;124;124mwith crit(j) < λ.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIn each case, let κ = crit(j) and λ = sup_{n<ω} jⁿ(κ) (so j(λ) = λ).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Key observation.** For I_1 and I_0, the embedding depends only on V_{λ+1} (for[0m[38;2;124;124;124mI_1) or L(V_{λ+1}) (for I_0). Any forcing that does not change V_{λ+1} preserves[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe embedding. Under GCH below λ, λ is a strong limit and |V_λ| = λ, so a <λ⁺-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed forcing does not add subsets of V_λ, hence does not change V_{λ+1} = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mP(V_λ). Since L(V_{λ+1}) is constructed by transfinite recursion from V_{λ+1} [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(which is absolute between transitive models with the same V_{λ+1} and the same [0m[38;2;124;124;124mordinals), such a forcing also does not change L(V_{λ+1}).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSimilarly, for I_3, any forcing that does not change V_λ preserves the embedding[0m[38;2;124;124;124mj: V_λ → V_λ.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Forcing construction.** We force GCH in two stages:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Stage 1: GCH below λ.** Let P be the canonical GCH forcing below λ — a set [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mforcing (a reverse Easton iteration below λ) that forces 2^α = α⁺ for every [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mregular cardinal α < λ. Since P is a set of rank ≤ λ, we have P ∈ V_{λ+1}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEach condition p ∈ P has rank < λ, so p ∈ V_λ. The embedding j acts on each [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcondition by elementarity (for I_3, j: V_λ → V_λ acts on p ∈ V_λ; for I_1, j: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mV_{λ+1} → V_{λ+1} acts on p ∈ V_λ ⊆ V_{λ+1}; for I_0, j: L(V_{λ+1}) → L(V_{λ+1})[0m[38;2;124;124;124macts on p ∈ V_λ ∈ L(V_{λ+1})).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTo lift j through P, we use the **Silver master condition argument**:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Factor P as P_κ * P_{tail}, where P_κ is the forcing below the critical point [0m[38;2;124;124;124mκ and P_{tail} is the forcing from κ to λ.[0m
